  "description": "ROLTOE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C62 H62 Dy4 N9 O19 1+,6(C2 H3 N1),0.5(H2 O1),H1 O1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.596-5.159 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.80-176.22°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(NO3)(HL)4{(py)2C(OH)O}2](OH)·6CH3CN·0.5H2O (H3L = 2-((2-hydroxybenzylidene)amino)propane-1,3-diol; (py)2C(OH)2 = gem-diol form of di-2-pyridyl ketone); anal. C74H82Dy4N15O20.50. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
